  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Owning My Masters (Mastered) (2024), published by University of Michigan Press, has been cited 6 times. Beyond that, it is used in teaching and has been written about in The Conversation.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Owning My Masters (Mastered) by A.D. Carson was published by University of Michigan Press in 2024. It is part of the Tracking Pop series. Conceptually, the work connects to History. The book was recognised: ACLS Open Access Book Prize & Arcadia Open Access Publishing Award finalist (2026) \u2014 Multimodal.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 6 citations. Citations peaked in 2024 with 3 citing works. Notable citing venues include Traditions of Music and Dance. The citing authors are based in the United States.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">In teaching, it is discussed in 1 recorded lecture. It has been downloaded 35 times via OAPEN. It has also been written about for a general audience in The Conversation.</p>",
